  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/2B7850">Definition <span data-tag="2B7850">1.2.13.4</span> <span class="named">(Joyal <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/joyalpub">joyalpub</a>]</span>)</span>.</a>colimitlimit Let $\calC $ be an $\infty $-category and let $p: K \rightarrow \calC $ be an arbitrary map of simplicial sets. A <em>colimit</em> for $p$ is an initial object of $\calC _{p/}$ and a <em>limit</em> for $p$ is a final object of $\calC _{/p}$. </p>
